      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The last step follows since the derivative terms, evaluated at $ \\mu_x $, are really just constants. Further simplification is possible since, by the definition of a mean, $ E(x - \\mu_x) = 0 $, and $ E[(x - \\mu_x)^2] $ is the expected variance of $ x $, $ \\sigma^2(x) $. Thus, ignoring third- and higher-order terms,",
